                <pb facs="0740" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.4016/116: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-13T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                                1927—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2. For your information only. This morning a delegation, headed by Rabbi Wise and
                    representing the American Jewish Congress and other national Jewish
                    organizations, protested to the Secretary against alleged oppression of Jews in
                    Rumania and asked that this Government intercede with Rumanian Government.</p>
                <p>That part of, the press account of the interview which refers to the Secretary’s
                    reply to the delegation and which was textually approved by the Department is as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Secretary gave a lengthy and sympathetic hearing to the Delegation
                            and was deeply impressed with the gravity of the allegations submitted.
                            He promised to reply to the Delegation after making a careful study of
                            the considerations set forth. He added that of course he had every
                            sympathy with the ideals of religious liberty and of racial and cultural
                            equality.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
